  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with onboarding on September 10th. An idea submission phase for AI-enhanced data visualization tools was open until July 20th. The project reached a milestone with the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing for secure file sharing, celebrated on October 10th. A total budget of $2M has been approved for research, development, and marketing, with a specific $15,000 allocated for training programs starting next month. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated effective January next year."
